On June 13, 2026, at approximately 11:35 p.m., officers were responding to a call for service at an apartment building in the 2800 block of Dewdney Avenue when they located a male sleeping in the stairwell.
Officers woke the male and attempted to speak with him. As he stood, officers observed him reach for his waistband, where a firearm was visible. The suspect was quickly taken into custody without incident. Police seized the loaded firearm.
As a result of this investigation, 23 year-old Cody HENDERSON is charged with:
4 x Possession of Firearm or Ammunition Contrary to Prohibition Order [CC 117.01(1)];
Possession of a Load Prohibited/Restricted Firearm [CC 95(1)];
Possession of a Firearm Knowing its Possession is Unauthorized [CC 92(1)];
Carrying a Concealed Weapon [CC 90]; and
Careless Use of a Firearm, Weapon, Prohibited Device or Ammunition [CC 86(1)].
HENDERSON made his first appearance on these charges in Regina Provincial Court today (June 15, 2026).

A 30-year-old male is facing charges following a weapons-related incident involving a knife.
At approximately 5:55 p.m. on Friday, June 26, 2026, police were dispatched to a residence in the 1000 block of Robinson Street after receiving a report of a weapons offence. Initial information indicated an unknown male had approached a residence seeking help before entering the home and threatening the occupant with a knife.
Officers attended the scene and safely took the suspect into custody. The victim was not physically injured.
As a result of this investigation, 30 year-old Brennon DESJARLAIS is charged with:
Assault with a Weapon [CC 267(A)];
Break Enter and Commit [CC 348(1)(B)];
Obstruct Peace Officer [CC 129(A)];
4 x Forcible Confinement [CC 279(2)]; and
Fail to Comply with Condition of a Release Order [CC 145(5)(A)];
DESJARLAIS made his first appearance on these charges in Regina Provincial Court this morning on June 29, 2026.
